  "content": [
    {
      "text": "he refused to be comforted, Gen. 37:35. he refused, and said unto his master’s wife, Gen. 39:8. if thou refuse to let him go, Ex. 4:23 (8:2; 9:2; 10:4). How long refuse ye to keep my commandments, Ex. 16:28. Edom refused to give Israel passage, Num. 20:21. I have refused him … Lord seeth not as man, 1 Sam. 16:7. They … refused to walk in his law, Ps. 78:10. stone which the builders refused is become the head, Ps. 118:22. I have called, and ye refused, Prov. 1:24. Hear instruction … and refuse it not, Prov. 8:33. he that refuseth reproof erreth, Prov. 10:17. shame shall be to him that refuseth instruction, Prov. 13:18. He that refuseth instruction despiseth his own soul, Prov. 15:32. his hands refuse to labour, Prov. 21:25. if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured, Isa. 1:20. refuse the evil, and choose the good, Isa. 7:15 (2 Ne. 17:15). they have refused to receive correction … refused to return, Jer. 5:3. through deceit they refuse to know me, Jer. 9:6. evil people, which refuse to hear my words, Jer. 13:10. Rahel … refused to be comforted for her children, Jer. 31:15. they have refused my judgments, Ezek. 5:6.",
